# Both images build with the repo root as context (`docker build .` for the
# frontend, `docker build -f backend/Dockerfile .` for the backend), so this
# is the only .dockerignore Docker reads — a backend/.dockerignore would be
# silently ignored. Anything not excluded here is visible to COPY.

# Secrets — never let a local build bake them into an image layer
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
monitoring/secrets/

# Installed or generated on the host — the Dockerfiles install their own
**/node_modules
frontend/dist
**/npm-debug.log*

# Not used by either image
.git
.github
.claude
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
mobile
atlas
docs
terraform
monitoring
backend/tests
*.md
